# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# NOTE: a '#' only starts a comment at the beginning of a line. Written inline
# after a pattern, as in "config/api_keys.json  # your key", it becomes part of
# the pattern — so the line silently matches nothing and the secret it was
# written to protect gets committed. Every comment below is therefore on a line
# of its own. Keep it that way.
#
# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials and saved database logins
config/api_keys.json
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# The enrolled voiceprint — a vector derived from your voice, so it is a biometric
# even though no audio is stored. It also unlocks the microphone, so it does not
# belong in a repository any more than a key does.
config/voiceprint.json
# Downloaded speaker-embedding weights for Voice ID (ECAPA-TDNN)
config/models/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp account,
# not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# An affect reading is a record of how you were doing, when, and how often. It is
# the most personal thing this app writes and the least obviously personal by
# filename — it looks like state, the way long_term.json looks like state.
memory/affect_state.json
# The initiative log records when JARVIS chose to speak, whether you answered,
# and how long you had been quiet. Boring individually; a pattern of
# availability, if you would rather it lived nowhere near a repo.
memory/initiative_state.json
# Routines are your personal schedules (wake-ups, briefings) — same rule.
memory/routines.json
# Conversation history is a record of what was actually said.
memory/conversation_history.json
# Belt and braces. An earlier build resolved the base directory without the
# memory/ segment and dropped these in the repository root, where they are
# perfectly visible to `git add .` and perfectly easy to miss in review. The
# path is correct now; this is here so that a regression writes to an ignored
# location rather than a committed one.
/initiative_state.json
/affect_state.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
